WEBVTT

00:15:29.042 --> 00:15:30.851
I continue to look at other things

00:15:30.875 --> 00:15:34.059
and at people who said things
that I found really interesting.

00:15:34.083 --> 00:15:36.309
And when I can't come up with research,

00:15:36.333 --> 00:15:40.143
I go to philosophers and poets
who have a different way

00:15:40.167 --> 00:15:42.893
of trying to grapple
with the unexplainable.

00:15:42.917 --> 00:15:45.893
So Adam Phillips, this wonderful
English psychoanalyst,

00:15:45.917 --> 00:15:50.351
starts to talk about how trust
is a risk masquerading as a promise.

00:15:50.375 --> 00:15:52.018
I thought that was very beautiful.

00:15:52.042 --> 00:15:55.309
Then he said, "Trust is a word
that we often put too much trust in."

00:15:55.333 --> 00:15:56.684
(Laughter)

00:15:56.708 --> 00:15:58.518
AG: That sentence is self-defeating.

00:15:58.542 --> 00:16:01.393
EP: You know, then
Rachel Botsman talked about